 like the end of a story is, in fact, the beginning as Wilbur finds himself standing on a train platform with his mind â€œreverberating as if from some giant cosmic cymbal crashâ€. A train arrives and a woman disembarks and introduces herself as Agnes. She is, she says, the ghost of a bookseller who once ran a shop Wilbur visited as a child. She will be guiding him in a voyage through his past, pausing at formative moments including his brotherâ€™s premature death and Wilbur and Maggieâ€™s honeymoon in Venice. â€œThis is death,â€ Agnes tells him. â€œWhere your life flashes before your eyes. This is how it happens. Fast and slow. Like life â€¦ â€</p> <a href="https://www.theguardian.com/books/2026/jul/23/the-midnight-train-by-matt-haig-audiobook-review-a-cosy-feelgood-journey">Continue reading...</a>ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;vtWHsDhqOWCsMkL9xuTRoRfk_UCFNJ2-wRxFq4qX5ysƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx9ni:///sha-256;7itFqN1U2EYXRlbx-PaF2uQLeBicgtrYoeWQXfNuAeEƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;6JZ9H_bnAdJURBUrbt6rEQnEkJs7ZvcokzEa4FgnquQƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;HIUFw1HpTXruBYrR4Hmx7angjlj16ixDidWQIZY8uJQƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkefalseƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;EDjwVC-VkDmVJa-ThGbG8lsEkvYoHtt631M6nUwkk9Qƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkdtrueƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;3oDjV053WBZVOmLRycCCHONOnA4SVv7EgfYZbgk_RQ0ƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;37vIgs6tY4T1uwXl-6ooFlkMUAVJzmQ5b3LNEXb8mPkƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightduni